  {
   "id": "K14TnDmOAwAJ",
   "from": "Vincent van Hees",
   "author": "8d92e34685fbc6bd",
   "date": "2016-11-07T20:11:47Z",
   "subject": "Re: [GGIR] Parameters for nonwear time",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Natalie,</div><div><br></div><div>Your interpretation is correct.</div><div><br></div><div>The 50 versus 150 threshold for the ranger criteria (racriter) may have been an incorrect copy/paste of the parameters used in my earlier papers on the GENEA accelerometer which did have less noise.</div><div>However, my understanding now is that this racriter is mostly redundant. I added it as an intuitive safety check, but non-wear detection seems to work equally well without it.</div><div><br></div><div>Finally, it may be worth mentioning in relation to my code comments &quot;adjustment needed...&quot; that the Actigraph data I have seen indicate that the 0.013 criteria works fine. Further, UKBiobank has been using the 0.013 criteria in their copy of my non-wear detection algorithm for their Axivity data.</div><div><br></div><div>Best, Vincent</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On 7 November 2016 at 20:50, Natalie Colabianchi <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">cola...@umich.edu</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">hi Vincent,</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks for all your good work on this program.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I wanted to verify the parameters that are used to define\r\nnon-wear.  Within your code, I\r\ncan see that the parameters vary by device (code pasted below).<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0pt\">There are a\r\nfew published papers that state that the parameters for non-wear for a\r\nGENEActiv device processed in GGIR are as follows. “<span style=\"color:black;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Grande&quot;;font-size:10.5pt\">A time window was classified as non-wear time if, for at least two out\r\nof the three axes, the standard deviation was less than 13 m<em><span style=\"padding:0in;border:1pt windowtext\">g</span></em><span> </span>and the value range was less than 50 m<em><span style=\"padding:0in;border:1pt windowtext\">g</span></em>.<span>”  </span></span>Taken\r\nfrom : da Silva IC, van Hees VT, Ramires VV, Knuth AG, Bielemann RM, Ekelund U,\r\nBrage S, Hallal PC. Physical activity levels in three Brazilian birth cohorts\r\nas assessed with raw triaxial wrist accelerometry. Int J Epidemiol. 2014\r\nDec;43(6):1959-68. doi: 10.1093/ije/dyu203. PubMed PMID: 25361583; PubMed\r\nCentral PMCID: PMC4276065.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal;margin-bottom:0pt\"><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal;margin-bottom:0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal;margin-bottom:0pt\">This seems to contradict what is stated in the code as the default.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal;margin-bottom:0pt\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal;margin-bottom:0pt\">I\r\nam writing up the methods for data that used ActiGraphs so I want to be sure\r\nthat I correctly defined the parameters in the case where we did not change your\r\ndefaults.  I have written:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal;margin-bottom:0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"color:black;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:12pt\">Nonwear time was identified when the standard deviation (SD) was\r\nless than 13 mg for 2 of the 3 axes <b>and</b>\r\nif value range of <b>each accelerometer\r\naxis</b> was less than <b>150</b> mg,\r\ncalculated for moving windows of 60 minutes with 15- minute increments.  </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal;margin-bottom:0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal;margin-bottom:0pt\">Is this correct?<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal;margin-bottom:0pt\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal;margin-bottom:0pt\">Natalie</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal;margin-bottom:0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal;margin-bottom:0pt\">g.getmeta.R excerpt – <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal;margin-bottom:0pt\"><a href=\"https://github.com/cran/GGIR/blob/af333fe33917552744aebb5551475b309beaa96b/R/g.getmeta.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/cran/GGIR/blob/af333fe33917552744aebb5551475b309beaa96b/R/g.getmeta.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792491627220000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2vKelQ66cUQPQgwrOg7Vur\">https://github.com/cran/GGIR/blob/af333fe33917552744aebb5551475b309beaa96b/R/g.getmeta.R</a><u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal;margin-bottom:0pt\"><br></p><table style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px;border-collapse:collapse;box-sizing:border-box\"><tbody style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><tr style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><td style=\"line-height:20px;overflow:visible;padding-right:10px;padding-left:10px;font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;vertical-align:top;white-space:pre-wrap;box-sizing:border-box\"><span style=\"color:rgb(150,152,150);box-sizing:border-box\">#non-wear criteria are monitor specific</span></td></tr><tr style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><td style=\"border-style:solid;border-color:rgb(238,238,238);width:50px;text-align:right;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.298039);line-height:20px;padding-right:10px;padding-left:10px;font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;vertical-align:top;border-right-width:1px;white-space:nowrap;min-width:50px;box-sizing:border-box\"></td><td style=\"line-height:20px;overflow:visible;padding-right:10px;padding-left:10px;font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;vertical-align:top;white-space:pre-wrap;box-sizing:border-box\">            <span style=\"color:rgb(167,29,93);box-sizing:border-box\">if</span> (<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">mon</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(167,29,93);box-sizing:border-box\">==</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,134,179);box-sizing:border-box\">1</span>) {</td></tr><tr style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><td style=\"border-style:solid;border-color:rgb(238,238,238);width:50px;text-align:right;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.298039);line-height:20px;padding-right:10px;padding-left:10px;font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;vertical-align:top;bord